error: `v` is bound by a test, and seen only where that test is known to have held
 --> what_a_test_binds_is_not_seen_by_the_calls_other_arguments.fn:7:30
  |
7 | first(r) -> pick(r is Ok(v), v)
  |                              ^ not known to hold here
  |
  = help: a test's names go along `&`, not into a call's arguments: `r is Ok(v) & v < 100`
  = help: a test binds along its `&` chain, into `then`, into its clause from a guard, for the lines below its `else` line, and into its arm from an arm's pattern; past an `|` only what both sides bind, and nothing under `!` or in `else`
